WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.290
As the final season of Game of Thrones came
to a close, there were plenty of characters

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.300
left behind.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.130
Surprisingly, not all of them are dead just
forgotten while fan favorites fought off the

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:10.890
Long Night and rode around on dragons.

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:11.890
Daario Naharis

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:16.100
Long before sparks flew between Jon Snow and
Daenerys Targaryen, the Dragon Queen had another

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.730
lover, and we're not talking about the dearly
departed Khal Drogo.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:24.020
Daario Naharis was at one time a lieutenant
of a sellsword company called the Second Sons,

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:28.010
who proved his loyalty to Dany by killing
his commanders and taking control of the group

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:29.010
in her name.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.010
Why?

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:31.730
Because he had a big old crush on the Breaker
of Chains.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.510
"We had philosophical differences."

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:35.690
"Over what?"

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:36.720
"Your beauty."

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.580
"It meant more to me than it did to them."

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:43.520
As Dany and her army took over the cities
of Slaver's Bay, Daario got more and more

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.410
flirty, eventually earning himself a place
in her bed.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.880
As a queen, however, Dany's marriage would
have to be a political one, so as much as

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.760
Daario's pretty boy looks amused her, Dany
never quite returned his affection.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:57.480
This is why she left him behind in Essos to
help rule in her stead, breaking her ties

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.510
with him at Tyrion's prompting, and leaving
Daario lovesick on another continent for the

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:05.059
events of the final season… which probably
worked out for the best.

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:06.059
Nymeria

00:01:06.059 --> 00:01:09.090
Remember back when the most heartbreaking
thing about Game of Thrones was a scene straight

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:10.090
out of Old Yeller?

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:14.130
Back in season one, when Arya was somehow
even smaller than she is now, she and Sansa

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:18.099
got along about as well as cats and dogs,
but they both loved their overgrown direwolf

00:01:18.099 --> 00:01:19.099
puppies.

00:01:19.099 --> 00:01:23.130
They were heartbroken when Sansa's wolf, Lady,
was put down and Arya's, Nymeria, was sent

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:25.569
away after justifiably biting Prince Joffrey.

00:01:25.569 --> 00:01:29.779
Each of the Stark children had their own direwolf
at one point, most succumbing to the same

00:01:29.779 --> 00:01:31.509
tragic fates of their masters.

00:01:31.509 --> 00:01:35.579
As of the last episode, Ghost is still alive,
finally getting the pets he deserved from

00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:39.710
Jon Snow, and somewhere in the Riverlands,
Nymeria is still out there hunting.

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:47.169
Arya ran into the now-wild direwolf and her
newfound pack on her way back to Winterfell.

00:01:47.169 --> 00:01:51.069
"Nymeria?"

00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:54.469
As cool as it would have been for Arya to
have returned home with both sick assassin

00:01:54.469 --> 00:01:57.869
skills and a giant wolf, Nymeria had her own
family now.

00:01:57.869 --> 00:02:01.210
As much as she wanted to, Arya wasn't about
to take her away from them.

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:02.210
Meera Reed

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:05.149
Without Meera Reed, Bran wouldn't have made
it back to Winterfell in order to reveal the

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:07.060
great big secret of the series.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.410
Meera was tough as nails and an uncanny archer.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:13.280
While she was unable to save her brother from
dying at the hands of the wights, she does

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:17.540
deserve a few points for patiently sitting
in a creepy, cold cave during Bran's trips

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:21.739
into the past, shattering a White Walker with
a spear, and getting the Three-Eyed Raven

00:02:21.739 --> 00:02:23.540
back to Winterfell in one piece.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:27.180
In the end, though, the only thing she gets
from Bran is a blank look and a half-hearted

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.290
thank you.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.930
"My brother died for you."

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:35.930
"Hodor and Jojon died for you."

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.540
"I almost died for you."

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:41.700
Understandably frustrated, Meera reminds Bran
of all the people who sacrificed themselves

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.159
to hold the door and save him.

00:02:43.159 --> 00:02:48.530
Of course, in response he counters that Bran
Stark did die long live the Three-Eyed Raven.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:53.120
After all that, Meera finally goes home, taking
a well deserved rest and staying out of the

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:54.950
ensuing drama of the final season.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:55.950
Ed Sheeran

00:02:55.950 --> 00:03:00.489
In a rather controversial cameo, British pop
sensation Ed Sheeran appeared as a soldier

00:03:00.489 --> 00:03:05.569
during the seventh season, sharing a fireside
meal with Arya and treating her to a song.

00:03:05.569 --> 00:03:09.840
Actress Maisie Williams was apparently more
than a little starstruck, but alas, Sheeran's

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.290
character wasn't destined to stick around.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:16.379
When his character "Eddie" appeared, he was
part of the Lannister forces sent to the Riverlands

00:03:16.379 --> 00:03:20.480
after Arya's brutal assassination of Lord
Walder Frey and most of his house.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:24.290
Unfortunately for Eddie, we know that those
in gold and red armor eventually met with

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:29.310
a fiery fate on the Goldroad when Dany, the
Dothraki, and Drogon absolutely destroyed

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:30.310
them in battle.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:34.019
Remember those eerie shots of men turning
to ash under the incredible heat of dragon

00:03:34.019 --> 00:03:35.019
fire?

00:03:35.019 --> 00:03:37.420
Poor Ed Sheeran probably ruined his singing
voice screaming for his life.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:38.430
The good news?

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:42.359
Thanks to a conversation about "Eddie the
Ginger" in Season 8's first episode, we do

00:03:42.359 --> 00:03:44.879
know that he survived his encounter with Drogon.

00:03:44.879 --> 00:03:46.569
Just not in a particularly pleasant way.

00:03:46.569 --> 00:03:48.739
"Came back with his face burnt right off.

00:03:48.739 --> 00:03:50.420
He's got no eyelids now."

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:51.420
Hot Pie

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:54.829
Of all the minor characters in Game of Thrones,
none are as beloved as Hot Pie, who earned

00:03:54.829 --> 00:03:59.319
his nickname with baking skills that are almost
as legendary as Arya's ability to get revenge.

00:03:59.319 --> 00:04:03.660
He made Arya a loaf of adorable, slightly
malformed direwolf bread before she departed

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.829
with the Hound, and stole our hearts with
carbs.

00:04:05.829 --> 00:04:10.870
When Arya returned to Westeros in season 7,
she briefly reunited with Hot Pie at the crossroads

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:11.870
inn.

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:15.900
After thoroughly enjoying a few tasty treats,
he got Arya up to speed on all the big news,

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.780
like how Jon Snow somehow became King in the
North, which was one of the reasons why she

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:24.270
ultimately decided to return to Winterfell,
which led directly to her saving the entire

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:26.940
world, which isn't a bad contribution to the
series.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:30.310
She does give him one piece of solid advice
before she leaves, though:

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.440
"Take care of yourself Hotpie.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.000
Try not to get yourself killed."

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.000
"I won’t.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.560
I’m like you Aree…

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:38.840
I'm a survivor!"

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.941
Fighting the dead and taking on evil queens
aren't exactly playing to his skillset, so

00:04:42.941 --> 00:04:45.539
it makes sense that we didn't see him return
in season eight.

00:04:45.539 --> 00:04:49.669
But hey, Hot Pie might be the only person
in Westeros who actually got a normal job

00:04:49.669 --> 00:04:51.510
at the end of all this.

